{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Taken from Jerusalem, [Cm]a young man far from [Fm7]home
Babylon had golden halls [Bb7sus4]and gods of wood and stone
They [Eb]set the king's food on his [Cm]table, poured the king's own wine
But [Fm7]Daniel resolved in his heart
[Bb7sus4]Not to defile him[Eb]self
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Three times a day he got down on his knees and [Cm]prayed
Giving thanks to his God
[Fm7]Just as he had always done
Kings [Bb7sus4]may rise and kings may fall
He kept [Eb]on praying through it [Cm]all
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [Eb]king dreamed of a statue made of [Cm]gold and iron and clay
A [Fm7]stone not cut by human hands came [Bb7sus4]and broke it all away
[Eb]Daniel blessed the God of heav[Cm]en who knows what lies in the dark
He [Fm7]changes times and seasons
He re[Bb7sus4]moves kings and sets up kings
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]At Belshazzar's feast a hand wrote letters [Cm]on the wall
The [Fm7]cups of gold were shaking [Bb7sus4]and the king began to fall
You have [Eb]been weighed on the scales and [Cm]found too light
And the [Fm7]kingdom ended in [Bb7sus4]the dark of that same night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Three times a day he got down on his knees and [Cm]prayed
Giving thanks to his God
[Fm7]Just as he had always done
Kings [Bb7sus4]may rise and kings may fall
He kept [Eb]on praying through it [Cm]all
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
They [Eb]threw him in the lions' den and [Cm]sealed it with a ring
And [Fm7]sleep fled from the palace, [Bb7sus4]sleep fled from the king
At [Eb]the first light of dawn the king got up and [Cm]hurried to the lions' den
[Fm7]My God sent his angel and shut [Bb7sus4]the mouths of the li[Eb]ons
{end_of_bridge}

